        "abstract": "The major objective of paper is to contribute to solve of problems of machining (technological operation - turning) of wood plastic composite (material with natural reinforcement and matrix from plastic). During turning with tools with big nose radius and positive geometry, the spindle speed n (from 450 min<sup xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">-1</sup> to 1400 min<sup xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">-1</sup>) and feed rate f (from 0.1 to 0.61 mm) were changed. Output from measured data (Rvk, Rk, Rpk, Mr, and Mr<sub xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">2</sub> probability descriptors) is Abbott-Firestone curve.",
